.SS Retrieving Files With Privilege Escalation
After logging into the remote host, using the administrator account (\fCroot\fP), to collect files starting with '/etc/host' and store them in the \fCdest\fP directory, specify the options as follows:
.PP
.EX
gm-gather -u root --ssh-user=user --pack -v '/etc/^host.*' dest
.EE
.PP
The meaning of each option is as follows:
.IP \(bu 2
Specify \fC-u root\fP to retrieve files under \fC/etc\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Since root cannot ssh login directly, log in once as \fCuser\fP, then use sudo to become the privileged user and retrieve the files
.IP \(bu 2
Use \fC--pack\fP to attempt retrieval including symbolic links
.IP \(bu 2
Use \fC-v\fP to display detailed logs
.IP \(bu 2
Specify the retrieval file pattern '/etc/^host.*' in \fCSRC\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Specify the output destination directory as \fCdest\fP
.PP
An example of executing the above command is as follows.
.PP
.EX
$ gm-gather -u root --ssh-user=user --pack -v '/etc/^host.*' dest
