.SH Limitations and Notes
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCSRC\fR regular expressions follow Python \fCre\fR specifications, so they may contain locale-dependent metacharacters. Use explicit flags as needed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--pack\fR requires \fCtar\fR and \fCgzip\fR to be installed on the remote. If unavailable, it exits with an error.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--follow-symlinks\fR only works when combined with \fB--pack\fR. If the remote tar command does not support resolving links, symbolic links cannot be retrieved.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Existing files in the local destination will be overwritten. There is no differential retrieval capability.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--password\fR is specified on the command line and may be recorded in shell history. Exercise caution when handling it.
.IP "\(bu" 2
UNC paths on Windows hosts (e.g., \fC//srv/share\fR) can be specified, but they are normalized to paths containing underscores during saving.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Sending \fBSIGINT\fR during a long collection may result in only some hosts being collected. Check the logs and output, and rerun if necessary.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Integrity checks (such as hash verification) for acquired files are not implemented. Verify separately as needed.

